#
# Conformance case: foundation/relcomp-under-mediated
# AC: foundation lowering — OntoUML RelComp discipline (issue #503).
#
# Reproduces reasoning_lint.relator_mediation in its logic-layer reading: a
# concrete relator must mediate at least two DISTINCT relata (the logic layer
# counts distinct logic:mediates relata ≥2; the gUFO functional/non-functional
# end-weighting is a downcast concern checked in Task 6, not here).
#   * ex:Marriage   — a concrete logic:Relator (no logic: subclass) with ONLY ONE
#     logic:mediates relatum (ex:Spouse1) → logic:RelComp.
#   * ex:Employment — a well-formed concrete logic:Relator with TWO DISTINCT
#     logic:mediates relata (ex:Employer, ex:Employee) → trips nothing (negative
#     control).
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the schema facts
# (the Relator puns + the logic:mediates edges) are duplicated there in the named
# world ex:schema; these declarations are the program axioms the projections need.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/relcomp-under-mediated/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Schema: an under-mediated relator and a well-formed one (also world facts in input.nq).
ex:Marriage   a logic:Relator ;
    logic:mediates ex:Spouse1 .
ex:Employment a logic:Relator ;
    logic:mediates ex:Employer, ex:Employee .
